# Cloud Card Baking Pipelines

Status: incubation workflow and future-skill candidate

Current revision: `incubation-r18`

Decision date: 2026-08-02

This document separates the two Cubeless cloud-card authoring routes. They
share the same light-packed texture family, but they solve different visual
problems and must not share framing or tiling gates.

This is the canonical working specification, not a finished Codex skill.
Continue revising it from production evidence. Promote it to a formal skill
only after the promotion gates in this document pass and the user explicitly
approves promotion.

## Lifecycle and change policy

Treat a rule marked as fixed as binding for the current revision, not
permanently immutable. Future revisions may change it through the following
process:

1. Record the reason and affected pipeline in the revision history.
2. Preserve accepted source art, prompts, manifests, and QA reports; do not
   silently overwrite an approved asset version.
3. Create a new asset or workflow revision for changed output.
4. Re-run every affected source, basis, packing, seam, and Unreal handoff gate.
5. Record metric changes and any migration or compatibility consequence.

Every generated set must be traceable from immutable source calls through
normalization, optional harmonization, basis projection, packing, and final
review. A current canonical path may point to a newer derivative only when the
older hash remains available under an explicit provenance filename.

## Pipeline names

| Pipeline | Korean name | Primary use | Repetition contract |
|---|---|---|---|
| Single Cloud Baking Pipeline | 단일 구름 베이킹 파이프라인 | One isolated hero, character, or showcase cloud | One self-contained card; horizontal tiling is not required |
| Distant Horizon Cloud Baking Pipeline | 원경 구름 베이킹 파이프라인 | A long cloud bank placed around the horizon | Two compatible 4096x1024 variants in the fixed cycle `A -> B -> A -> B` |

The distant pipeline is not a replacement or quality tier for the single-cloud
pipeline. Select the pipeline from the intended composition before source-art
generation starts.

## Stability map

### Fixed for `incubation-r13`

- The two public pipeline names and their routing distinction.
- Single-cloud Hunyuan work uses mesh-only generation with `texture=false`;
  its SDF authoring resolution remains `256 x 256 x 256`.
- The current Single Cloud packed-card candidate profile is R6 at
  `4096 x 2560`. It preserves the upper and side silhouette and softens only
  the broad, downward-facing lowest exterior silhouette.
- Distant-horizon sets contain exactly two `4096 x 1024` variants in the fixed
  cycle `A -> B -> A -> B`; no C variant is generated.
- The current Distant Horizon candidate uses schema 8 pairwise seam treatment:
  only the outer 8 percent of each side is blended in seam coordinates, while
  the central 84 percent remains the direct R6 result.
- Distant source art uses the exact compositing background `RGB(0,17,38)`.
- Every variant delivers the same three-map packed family:
  `BeautyRGBA`, `StaticBasisRGBA`, and `LightDataRGBA`.
- Source masks, directional basis masks, packed alpha, and cross-tile seams
  must pass machine-readable gates.
- Accepted source calls and pre-correction derivatives remain preserved.
- Cards placed through `/Game/Study/SKY_Cloud/StaticCloudCard` use the shared
  manual-exposure and `MPC_CloudBakeSky` runtime contract defined below.
- Card colour uses the SkyDome-owned four-stop remap contract. The SkyDome owns
  four source colours for each Day/Twilight/Night palette and publishes all
  twelve source colours, the shared ramp shape, and the `2°` Twilight-full /
  `30°` Day-full transition elevations. Each card material resolves the live
  time-of-day blend from `SkyAtmosphereLightDirection` index 0. The cached
  current four colours remain only for invalid-live fallback and compatibility.
  The sky-wisp branch is outside this revision and remains unchanged.
- Card backlighting is a SkyDome-owned, material-native analytic response. It
  uses the live sun/view phase, `LightDataRGBA.B` extinction, packed-normal
  slopes from `LightDataRGBA.RG`, and `BeautyRGBA.A` only as an inside-
  silhouette gate. It changes radiance only; packed alpha, the underside-only
  R6 silhouette rule, source textures, and the unchanged Wisp branch remain
  outside the effect.

### Intentionally tunable during incubation

- ImageGen prompt wording, macro-group counts, skyline rhythm, and far-layer
  composition.
- Normalization thresholds, edge feathering, mantle extraction, optical-depth
  shaping, and packed-map compression choices.
- A/B exposure and color harmonization method and strength.
- Directional basis projection blur radius, gain limits, and basis weighting.
- Numeric QA thresholds after enough accepted examples establish better
  tolerances.
- Unreal card geometry, material controls, placement spacing, and blending,
  provided the fixed A/B order and current asset contracts remain valid.

When a tunable value changes, store it in the generated report or manifest.
Do not rely on conversation history as the only record.

## 1. Single Cloud Baking Pipeline

Use this route when the silhouette of one cloud is the subject: a rabbit head,
a hero cumulus, or one authored cloud mass that must remain recognizable from
its own card.

### Contract

1. Author one isolated cloud silhouette and preserve a clear frame margin.
2. When the cloud needs a real three-dimensional volumetric source, use the
   Hunyuan mesh route:
   - mesh only, with `texture=false`;
   - immutable original GLB;
   - glTF `X/right, Y/up, Z/forward` converted to volume
     `X/right, Y/forward, Z/up`;
   - fixed `256 x 256 x 256` SDF authoring;
   - no Blueprint pitch compensation.
3. Stage and art-direct the cloud in the Unreal volumetric material when a
   volumetric source is used.
4. Bake one final card set from the approved view.
5. Deliver one Beauty source, three pixel-aligned directional basis sources,
   one manifest, and the three packed textures:
   - `BeautyRGBA`;
   - `StaticBasisRGBA`;
   - `LightDataRGBA`.
6. Deliver one material instance and, when requested, one child Blueprint for
   that cloud.

The binding Hunyuan/SDF details live in
`SourceArt/Clouds/Cumulus_01/HunyuanSDF10/HUNYUAN_SDF_PIPELINE_CONTRACT.md`.
The Hunyuan branch is used only when three-dimensional source geometry is
needed; it is not required for every already-approved 2D cloud source.

### R6 packed-card candidate contract

The current Single Cloud candidate output is `4096 x 2560`. R6 applies an
underside-only exterior treatment: it may soften the broad lowest silhouette
that faces the viewer and reads as the cloud base, but it must preserve crisp
upper lobes, side contours, ears, peaks, narrow appendages, and internal
recesses. It must not apply a uniform feather around the whole silhouette.

Opacity keeps coverage and density as separate signals. `BeautyRGBA.A` is
coverage; `LightDataRGBA.B` is an independent density proxy. The material
computes a Beer-Lambert density response, protects pixels that are both
high-coverage and high-density as a dense core, and applies density separation
to the lower-density mantle without turning dense interiors translucent. The
current defaults are `DensityOpacityBlend=1.0`,
`DensityOpticalDepthScale=6.0`, and `DensityOpacityFloor=0.06`.

The following six R6 candidate assets passed the combined alpha, density, mip,
padding, silhouette, and packed-family machine QA on 2026-08-01:

- `RabbitCloudHead_R6UnderFeather_ID112_4KCandidate`
- `WideCumulusBank_Bright_R6UnderFeather_ID112_4KCandidate`
- `HorizonCumulusChain_Bright_R6UnderFeather_ID112_4KCandidate`
- `ToweringCumulusMass_Bright_R6UnderFeather_ID112_4KCandidate`
- `WideCumulusBank_Natural_R6UnderFeather_ID112_4KCandidate`
- `LeaningCumulusTrail_Bright_R6UnderFeatherB60_ID112_4KCandidate`

`LeaningCumulusTrail_Bright` is the recorded exception: the full-strength R6
underside blend exceeded the silhouette-delta gate, so its accepted machine-QA
candidate uses the explicit B60, or 60-percent, underside blend. Do not hide
such per-asset exceptions behind a generic profile name.

### Single-cloud quality gates

- The intended hero silhouette remains identifiable at card-view distance.
- No cloud signal touches the texture frame.
- The Beauty and all basis masks remain pixel-aligned.
- The packed alpha is identical across the packed texture family.
- Dense core, translucent mantle, and scattering edge remain distinguishable.
- Review the card over both a dark matte and the target sky.
- Texture addressing remains Clamp unless a separate use case explicitly
  requires tiling.

## 2. Distant Horizon Cloud Baking Pipeline

Use this route for a long cloud band near the horizon. The authored subject is
the combined rhythm of many cloud groups and depth layers, not one landmark
cloud.

### Fixed production contract

- Variant count: exactly two, named `A` and `B`.
- Source and packed size per variant: `4096 x 1024`.
- Runtime/placement cycle: `A -> B -> A -> B`.
- Default source route: built-in ImageGen directly authors the final lit cloud
  card sources. Hunyuan, mesh texturing, and SDF generation are not part of the
  default distant-horizon route.
- Background: flat `RGB(0,17,38)` (`#001126`) with no sky gradient, horizon
  line, ground, stars, text, or watermark.
- The asset contains cloud signal only. Every outer frame pixel is background.
- The two variants must use different main-peak positions, valley depths,
  group widths, and far-layer phase.

### Required depth hierarchy

Each variant contains independently composed layers:

1. Main horizon shelf: low, connected, irregular medium and low-medium
   cumulus groups with bright neutral cores.
2. Mid/far belt: smaller, lower, softer, lower-contrast blue-gray groups seen
   behind and through the main valleys.
3. Vapor mantle: a wider translucent blue-gray region surrounding the dense
   cores.
4. Scattering envelope: a thin fading boundary that prevents an opaque
   cutout or carved-foam appearance.

The far belt must not be a scaled copy of the main shelf. Its silhouette,
horizontal phase, contrast, and spacing are authored independently.

### A/B macro-rhythm contract

- `A`: a calm rolling rhythm with approximately eight irregular groups and no
  central hero tower; the far belt is long and nearly continuous.
- `B`: an asymmetric rise-and-fall rhythm with approximately seven groups and
  wider low valleys; the far belt appears as two loose chains through those
  valleys.
- The first and last 8-10 percent of both variants stay low and quiet. They
  contain no unique landmark and taper to exact background before the frame.
- A and B are a fixed pair. Arbitrary `A -> A`, `B -> B`, or reordered
  sequences are not production placements.

### Distant-horizon deliverables

Each of A and B delivers:

- one normalized `4096 x 1024` Beauty source;
- upper-right, upper-left, and overhead directional basis sources;
- one ImageGen prompt record;
- one manifest;
- `BeautyRGBA`, `StaticBasisRGBA`, and `LightDataRGBA`;
- individual source and packed QA.

The set also delivers one shared `A-B-A-B` review image and one cross-tile QA
report covering both `A -> B` and `B -> A`.

### Distant-horizon quality gates

- Both sources and all packed textures are exactly `4096 x 1024`.
- Background and outer frame pixels match `RGB(0,17,38)` before packing.
- No frame contact or hard vertical edge exists.
- `A -> B` and `B -> A` pass RGB, alpha, premultiplied-color, and edge-slope
  seam checks.
- A and B do not share the same dominant peak positions or a recognizable
  short-period silhouette.
- A and B use one harmonized exposure and color-temperature family. Alternating
  brightness, cream/blue tint, or shadow saturation must not reveal the cycle.
- The far belt reads as farther, smaller, softer, lower, and lower-contrast
  than the main shelf.
- Review `A-B-A-B` at full size and at 50%, 25%, and 12.5% scale.
- Review over both dark navy and the target sky.
- Packed alpha equality and basis-mask alignment pass for both variants.

The single-tile `A -> A` or `B -> B` self-wrap report is not an approval gate
for this pipeline because those sequences are not valid placements. Use the
shared horizon-set QA and evaluate only `A -> B` and `B -> A`, including both
outer 8-percent density profiles. A self-wrap report may be retained only under
an explicitly non-authoritative review folder.

### Schema 8 pairwise seam-safe candidate

The current Distant Horizon candidate keeps the direct R6 packed result in the
central 84 percent of each `4096 x 1024` tile. Only the outer 8 percent on each
side is pairwise blended after one side is mirrored into seam coordinates.
Coverage and premultiplied Beauty color are blended as one seam contract;
`StaticBasisRGBA` and `LightDataRGBA` receive matching edge support. Every
fully transparent `LightDataRGBA` pixel must be exactly the neutral no-cloud
value `RGB(128,128,0)`, so transparent-padding neutral deviation is zero and
density never leaks into empty pixels.

Both verification layers are mandatory for A and B:

1. General packed-card alpha/density/mip/padding QA must pass for each variant.
2. Shared cross-tile QA must pass both `A -> B` and `B -> A`, including alpha,
   premultiplied color, boundary slope, edge-zone profile, and A/B diversity.

For the 2026-08-01 R8 candidate, edge-zone alpha-profile RMSE is `0.01731` for
`A -> B` and `0.02855` for `B -> A`, below the `0.08` limit. Transparent
`LightDataRGBA` padding deviation is `0` for both variants. The per-variant
general QA and the shared cross-tile QA both report all gates passing.

The preceding R7 attempt restored the full accepted-v02 alpha field over the
new packed data. It failed the required approval contract and must not be
promoted, imported as the current pair, or used as evidence that schema 8 can
be skipped. Preserve it only as rejection evidence. Passing R8 machine gates
still produces a candidate: visual review in the target sky and explicit user
approval remain mandatory before production acceptance or formal-skill
promotion.

### Unreal handoff

The initial Unreal representation is two sibling texture/material/Blueprint
variants placed in the fixed A/B cycle. Keep per-card texture addressing on
Clamp. Use X Wrap only if a later implementation changes to one continuous
mesh with continuous repeating UVs and revalidates the internal boundaries.

At BC7 with full mips, three packed `4096 x 1024` maps are approximately
16 MiB per variant, or approximately 32 MiB for the complete A/B set.

## Shared Unreal sky/card stabilization contract

This contract applies to both baking routes when their result is imported
through `/Game/Study/SKY_Cloud/StaticCloudCard`.

- `/Game/Study/SKY_Cloud/StaticCloudCard/SkyBake/BP_CloudBakeSkyDome` is the
  single writer for
  `/Game/Study/SKY_Cloud/StaticCloudCard/SkyBake/Data/MPC_CloudBakeSky`.
  It publishes the twelve Day/Twilight/Night card-ramp source colours, shared
  ramp shape, transition elevations, cached current four colours, and the first
  external `DirectionalLight`/`SkyLight` found in the level. Plane cards are
  consumers, never MPC writers.
- In the normal path, both the sky and cloud-card materials read
  `SkyAtmosphereLightDirection` and
  `SkyAtmosphereLightIlluminanceOnGround` for `Atmosphere Sun Light` index 0.
  Direction and ground illuminance therefore update material-native in editor
  and at runtime without an editor Tick. Card materials also derive their live
  solar elevation from that direction and blend the three source palettes
  immediately, without waiting for a Blueprint refresh.
- The live card-colour payload contains the twelve source vectors
  `CB_CardRampDayColor0..3`, `CB_CardRampTwilightColor0..3`, and
  `CB_CardRampNightColor0..3`; the three shared shape scalars
  `CB_CardRampPosition1`, `CB_CardRampPosition2`, and
  `CB_CardRampSoftness`; and the transition scalars
  `CB_CardRampTwilightFullElevationDeg` and
  `CB_CardRampDayFullElevationDeg`. The cached compatibility vectors
  `CB_CardRampColor0..3` store the last SkyDome-resolved current palette and
  are selected only when the live atmosphere-light link is invalid. The legacy
  `CB_CloudLit*`/`CB_CloudShadow*` vectors remain only for the unchanged sky
  wisp compatibility path and are not inputs to the R10 card-colour remap.
- The remaining shared vectors are `CB_TODWeights`, `CB_SunDirectionWS`,
  `CB_SunFilterColor`, and `CB_SkyLightColor`. The remaining shared scalars
  are `CB_SkyEmissionScale`, `CB_SunIntensity`, `CB_SunTemperatureK`,
  `CB_SunUseTemperature`, `CB_SkyLightIntensity`, `CB_StateValid`, and
  `CB_AtmosphereSunLightValid`, plus the R11 card-backlight controls
  `CB_CardBacklightStrength`, `CB_CardBacklightStartDot`,
  `CB_CardBacklightPhasePower`, `CB_CardBacklightDensityScale`,
  `CB_CardBacklightNormalFloor`, and `CB_CardSilverLiningStrength`.
- The test level Post Process Volume and camera must both use Manual exposure,
  physical-camera exposure off, and exposure bias `-0.5`. This calibrated
  half-stop protection preserves bright-sky gradation without returning to
  adaptive exposure. A camera post-process
  override can supersede the PPV, so both settings are binding. Sky emission
  is controlled separately by `Sky Emission Scale`, whose default is `1.0`.
- For a valid `Atmosphere Sun Light` index 0, card direction and ground
  illuminance and the Day/Twilight/Night card palette remain material-native
  and react without a BP Tick. Moving the external sun therefore requires no
  `RefreshFromSceneLights` call. `Refresh From Scene Lights` is reserved for
  rediscovering/caching scene lights and updating invalid-live fallback state.
  Construction Script and BeginPlay initialize that cache.
- Live card-palette weights use `sin(elevation)`. With the default
  `CardRampTwilightFullElevationDeg=2.0` and
  `CardRampDayFullElevationDeg=30.0`, positive elevation blends Twilight to Day
  over `2°..30°`, negative elevation mirrors the same range into Night, and
  Twilight is the remaining normalized weight. Day is full at `+30°`, Night is
  full at `-30°`, and the near-horizon interval remains fully Twilight.
- The sky sphere remains at scale `400,400,400` with shadow casting disabled.
- `M_StaticCloudCard` remains Unlit/AlphaComposite. It transforms
  the live atmosphere direction (or cached `CB_SunDirectionWS` fallback) from
  World to Tangent space, then flips tangent Y because the packed LightData Y
  axis follows image-row direction. `StaticBasisRGBA` R/G/B are dynamically
  weighted upper-right/upper-left/overhead lobes. The packed normal uses its
  full XYZ vector, including solar elevation, rather than only a planar
  direction.
- Active relight defaults are `AmbientStrength=0.85`,
  `StaticBasisStrength=0.45`, `LightDataStrength=0.25`, and
  `NormalLightStrength=0.75`. Shared material-only defaults are
  `SceneLightingBlend=1.0`, `SkyPaletteInfluence=0.65`,
  `SceneIntensityScale=1.0`, `SunIntensityReference=10.0`, and
  `SkyLightInfluence=0.35`, with `SceneBasisInfluence=0.90` and
  `SceneDirectionInfluence=0.70`.
- The shared coverage/density opacity defaults are
  `DensityOpacityBlend=1.0`, `DensityOpticalDepthScale=6.0`, and
  `DensityOpacityFloor=0.06`. Child assets may carry a documented candidate
  exception such as Single Cloud R6 B60 source blending, but must not silently
  override this runtime material contract.
- The material contract is authored once in `M_StaticCloudCard` and inherited
  by every descendant MI. Actor defaults are authored once in
  `BP_StaticCloudCard`, but every already-saved descendant cloud BP CDO must
  also be normalized explicitly to `AmbientStrength=0.85`,
  `StaticBasisStrength=0.45`, `LightDataStrength=0.25`, and
  `NormalLightStrength=0.75`; a parent-default change alone does not clear
  legacy child overrides. Preserve child-specific tint, alpha, texture, and
  layout overrides.
- Saved materials, Blueprints, MPC, and maps must contain no UnrealMCP runtime
  reference. UnrealMCP is an authoring-only transport.

### R10 live four-stop card-colour remap contract

`BP_CloudBakeSkyDome` owns the artist-facing source palettes. Each time band
has four independent `LinearColor` values:

- `CardRampDayColor0..3`;
- `CardRampTwilightColor0..3`;
- `CardRampNightColor0..3`.

Twilight remains the shared dawn-and-dusk band because solar elevation alone
cannot distinguish whether the sun is rising or setting. The shared remap
shape defaults are `CardRampPosition1=0.32`, `CardRampPosition2=0.72`, and
`CardRampSoftness=0.25`; stop 0 and stop 3 remain the fixed 0 and 1 endpoints.
The lower softness avoids steepening the middle of each remap segment. The
Twilight interior defaults are `(0.446883, 0.171332, 0.293696)` and
`(0.805010, 0.421387, 0.352860)`, pulled 35 percent toward the endpoint line so
low-sun Beauty shoulders do not become repeated purple/peach bands.
The transition defaults are `CardRampTwilightFullElevationDeg=2.0` and
`CardRampDayFullElevationDeg=30.0`. The SkyDome publishes all twelve source
colours, those three shape scalars, and both transition elevations to the MPC.
Every card material reads `SkyAtmosphereLightDirection` index 0, derives live
solar elevation, and resolves each of its four stops immediately. A card never
writes the MPC.

`CB_CardRampColor0..3` remains a cached current palette for compatibility and
for the invalid-live path. It is not the normal-path time-of-day input. This
supersedes the R9 runtime transport that published only the resolved four
colours, while preserving R9 as revision history.

Every card BP defaults to `UseCustomCloudRamp=0`, which consumes the resolved
live SkyDome colours or their cached invalid-live fallback. Setting it to `1`
substitutes only the final `CustomCloudRampColor0..3` for that actor after the
global live/fallback selection. It does not create custom Day/Twilight/Night
source sets. Ramp positions, softness, packed directional response,
scene-light direction, and illuminance remain shared; the override is not a
second lighting system.

The remap consumes the existing Beauty luminance and the existing
`StaticBasisRGBA`/`LightDataRGBA` relight result, so this revision does not
require a Beauty, basis, or light-data rebake. It changes RGB only. Preserve
the accepted coverage/density alpha contract and the R6 rule that softness is
restricted to the broad, downward-facing lowest exterior silhouette; upper
lobes and side contours remain crisp. Existing low-density lower haze and
premultiplied-edge protections also remain in force.

### R11/R12 analytic card-backlight contract

`BP_CloudBakeSkyDome` owns six artist-facing card-backlight scalars and
publishes them through `MPC_CloudBakeSky`:

| SkyDome variable | MPC parameter | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---:|---|
| `CardBacklightStrength` | `CB_CardBacklightStrength` | `0.58` | Overall forward-scattering response; `0` is an exact legacy-radiance rollback |
| `CardBacklightStartDot` | `CB_CardBacklightStartDot` | `0.50` | View/sun alignment where the lobe starts |
| `CardBacklightPhasePower` | `CB_CardBacklightPhasePower` | `1.40` | Angular focus around the sun |
| `CardBacklightDensityScale` | `CB_CardBacklightDensityScale` | `3.20` | Beer-Lambert extinction from packed density |
| `CardBacklightNormalFloor` | `CB_CardBacklightNormalFloor` | `0.06` | Bounded packed-normal recovery, gated to thin slopes |
| `CardSilverLiningStrength` | `CB_CardSilverLiningStrength` | `0.20` | Concentration from broad transmission (`0`) toward directional packed slopes (`1`) |

`M_StaticCloudCard` evaluates `dot(ViewDirectionWS, SunDirectionWS)` using the
live Atmosphere Sun Light 0 direction, with `CB_SunDirectionWS` only as the
invalid-live fallback. The forward lobe is multiplied by a Beer-Lambert
transmission from `LightDataRGBA.B`. A directional rim uses the packed
`LightDataRGBA.RG` slope and the sun direction in card tangent space; the
response is concentrated in low-density mantles rather than lifting the dense
core. A bounded exponential response reaches a finite, mildly overbright
four-stop-ramp peak, giving bloom energy without an unbounded additive halo.

The normal-floor correction and the radiance response are both multiplied by
`CardBacklightStrength`. Therefore a value of `0` restores the pre-R11 colour
path exactly. Opacity is not an input or output of this response: the material
keeps the existing coverage/density alpha and final premultiply path. No
Beauty, StaticBasis, or LightData rebake is required, and individual card BPs
remain MPC consumers with no new per-card lighting writer.

Promotion QA keeps the card camera fixed and the solar elevation identical,
then tests view/sun angles `15°`, `90°`, and `165°`. The `15°` image must show
thin-mantle transmission and directional silver lining while retaining a dark
dense core. The `90°` and `165°` images must lose the forward-scattering lobe.
All three must preserve the source silhouette, show no exterior halo or colour
bleed, add no dirty packages, and restore the exact light transform. The
2026-08-01 R11 review also preserved the test-map disk hash
`434159dbf73cbe8d0595721ea0362eb38192656ec9b5dbbeb9e8f5be4d08bee3`.

#### R12 natural backlight and sun-glow delta

- Dense cores receive a small strength-gated shade-floor recovery and a
  bounded proportional lift. Semi-alpha, low-density mantles receive a
  separate soft rim lift that does not hard-gate on packed slope, so Rabbit
  and other flat-normal bake families respond without turning into neon
  cut-outs. Both lifts preserve the resolved four-stop palette and local
  contrast; opacity and premultiply remain unchanged.
- `CardSilverLiningStrength` now defaults to `0.20`. The value is a
  concentration control, not a brightness control: `0` retains broad
  low-density transmission and `1` concentrates it on packed directional
  slopes. This prevents back-facing cards from becoming unnaturally dark.
- The sun halo replaces compact-support `smoothstep` with finite inner
  Gaussian-like and outer exponential lobes. `SunGlowRadius` remains a scale
  control rather than a cutoff boundary, the outer lobe is mildly
  desaturated, and the screen-style headroom lift never darkens the base sky.
  The inherited moon glow remains unchanged.
- Correct card-centred `15°`, `90°`, and `165°` captures verified that only
  the near-sun view receives strong forward scattering. At the approved
  `0.20` concentration, the `15°` Wide card measured core `145.98`, rim P95
  `169.04`, median `155.97`, and an `18.57` span; its back/front median ratio
  was `86.15%`, with no neon rim or flattened internal hierarchy.

#### R13 atmospheric shadow-floor delta

Natural backlit clouds keep a broadly illuminated atmospheric shadow body;
their deepest body tone does not become darker merely because the camera is
facing the sun. R13 therefore separates the stable body shadow from the
directional rim/transmission response:

- After packed/Beauty shade matching and before the four-stop ramp lookup,
  medium-to-dense body texels receive a shade-coordinate floor derived from
  `CardRampPosition1`. The accepted floor is
  `CardRampPosition1 * 0.46`, gated by backlight phase, strength, Beauty
  coverage, and packed density. Low-density exterior texels are excluded.
- The floor uses the existing live/custom four-stop ramp, so it follows every
  Day/Twilight/Night palette and per-card custom palette without adding a
  fixed grey colour, new texture, or new artist parameter. Already brighter
  shade coordinates are unchanged.
- Forward scattering, dense-core recovery, and semi-alpha rim transmission
  remain later, additive/monotonic layers. `CardBacklightStrength=0` still
  disables the floor and every transmission layer for exact legacy-radiance
  rollback. Opacity, silhouette, premultiply, packed textures, and Wisp are
  unchanged.
- In the fixed Wide-card `15°/90°/165°` review, `15°` versus `90°` measured
  p10 `-0.77Y`, p25 `-1.44Y`, median `-3.15Y`, and core `-0.18Y`. The accepted
  shadow-floor gate requires p10 and p25 to stay within `2Y` of the `90°`
  general-shadow view. The `15°` internal span remained `13.98Y`, preserving
  cloud hierarchy without a neon rim or destructive flattening.

#### R14 Hybrid Beauty/Density candidate

R14 is an isolated Single Cloud card candidate. It combines the useful broad
and deep local-form separation seen in
`/Game/Study/Sky_CloudV2/Textures/T_SkyCloudV2_CloudRef_0` with the existing
R6 Beauty/StaticBasis/LightData family. It does not repack or replace accepted
textures yet:

- `UseHybridBeautyDensity=0` retains the pre-R14 colour and opacity paths.
  `1` selects the candidate through a scalar 0/1 selector. This is not a
  material Static Switch and both paths remain in one compiled permutation.
- Beauty luminance supplies only two restrained form tiers. The reviewed
  defaults are `HybridBroadFormStrength=0.05` and
  `HybridDeepFormStrength=0.04`. Packed basis/normal/density moves the shade
  coordinate toward the live-light result with
  `HybridPackedInfluence=0.74`; the signed move is capped at `+/-0.12`, so the
  packed correction cannot erase the authored form or produce a hard two-tone
  split. The SkyDome four-stop ramp remains the final colour authority.
- The hybrid opacity path normalizes the Beer-Lambert response, uses
  `DensityResponsePower=0.85`, `DensityOpticalDepthScale=6.0`, and caps dense
  structural opacity at `DenseCoreMaxOpacity=0.94`. Beauty alpha remains the
  sole silhouette contract. Low-density, lower-edge, and mantle transparency
  therefore remain available while dense texels no longer form a 1.0-opacity
  plateau. Candidate MI and child-BP CDO values both enforce
  `OpacityScale=1`, `DensityOpacityBlend=1`, and depth `6`, because the base BP
  Construction Script republishes its CDO values to the runtime MID.
- The non-destructive assets live under
  `/Game/Study/SKY_Cloud/StaticCloudCard/HybridBeautyDensityR14`. The Wide and
  Rabbit candidate BPs preserve the exact source Beauty, StaticBasis, and
  LightData texture identities. The accepted master, MIs, BPs, and packed
  textures are not overwritten.
- `scripts/stage_hybrid_cloud_card_candidate_ue.py` authors, retunes, and
  verifies the isolated set. Verification requires material and BP compile
  error `0`, matching runtime-effective opacity values, exact source texture
  identity, and zero persisted UnrealMCP dependencies.
- `scripts/qa_cloud_card_alpha_mips.py` mirrors the HLSL floor clamp and
  normalization epsilon, evaluates the selected effective opacity values, and
  gates both `opacity >= 0.99` absence and the dense-core ceiling. Wide and
  Rabbit pass the full alpha/density/mip/padding suite at
  `output/cloud_card_hybrid_opacity_qa_20260802_r14final`.
- Four equal-view Day/Twilight/opposite-Twilight/Night A/B captures are at
  `output/cloud_card_hybrid_r14_review/lighting_tuned_074_005_004`. Independent
  visual review recommends this value set: it restores intermediate tones,
  preserves readable reverse-light and night form, and avoids making the
  `0.94` core look like an obviously transparent sheet. User visual acceptance
  is still required before replacing accepted assets or changing the packed
  schema.

The sky-dome Wisp is explicitly out of scope for R10. Do not rename, repurpose,
or reconnect its existing `Cloud*` variables, material parameters, or graph.

### R8 gameplay-height sky/card validation

The 2026-08-01 R8 live-level review uses two gameplay-height views rather than
only the authored showcase camera: the `PlayerStart` eye position at FOV 90,
and a second view offset laterally by `80,000 cm`, also at FOV 90. Each view is
captured under four directional-light states: day at `-60°`, twilight at
`-15°`, night at `+60°`, and twilight at the opposite azimuth (`+180°`). This
produces eight captures and tests both solar elevation response and the packed
card's horizontal light-direction response.

The response gate is evaluated only inside the union of projected cloud-card
AABBs. A comparison passes when RGB `MAE >= 0.75`, `P95 >= 3`, and at least
`5%` of ROI pixels change by more than `2` u8. Reported tuples below are
`MAE / P95 / changed>2`:

- Twilight versus opposite-azimuth twilight: PlayerStart
  `1.397 / 8.0 / 13.69%`; lateral `1.577 / 7.667 / 18.76%`.
- Day versus night: PlayerStart `142.965 / 162.333 / 100%`; lateral
  `152.688 / 167 / 100%`.

All four ROI comparisons pass. The eight source captures, contact sheet, and
machine-readable report are retained at:

- `output/cloud_bake_play_review_r8_20260801/CloudBakePlayReview_R8_20260801.png`
- `output/cloud_bake_play_review_r8_20260801/CloudBakePlayReview_R8_20260801.json`

This review also exposed and fixed the main sky material's live sun-direction
path. `SkyAtmosphereLightDirection` must feed `ComponentMask_8`, then
`Normalize_1`, while preserving the existing cached-direction fallback. Treat
that connection and fallback as a pipeline sky-contract QA item whenever the
sky material graph is rebuilt or migrated; card response alone is not enough
to prove the sky is using the same live light direction.

The machine result is a pass, but the remaining observations are art-review
flags, not automatic failures: daytime haze/paleness, nighttime cloud
readability, and visible A/B repetition still require user visual approval.
They must not be converted into production acceptance or a formal-skill
promotion without that explicit review.

Rebuild, normalize the canonical test level, verify the full contract, and
capture the review view:

```powershell
python .\scripts\stabilize_cloud_bake_sky_ue.py all --port 55561
```

Run the compile/readback verification stage without rebuilding the graphs:

```powershell
python .\scripts\stabilize_cloud_bake_sky_ue.py verify --port 55561
```

## Current deterministic toolchain

The current reusable implementation is intentionally kept as repository
scripts while the workflow is incubating:

| Stage | Script | Required record |
|---|---|---|
| Normalize A/B Beauty | `scripts/prepare_keilan_horizon_cloud_set.py` | preparation JSON |
| Harmonize A/B color | `scripts/harmonize_keilan_horizon_cloud_set.py` | immutable-input hashes and harmonization JSON |
| Project directional light | `scripts/project_keilan_basis_lighting.py` | basis projection JSON and exact-mask gates |
| Pack texture family | `scripts/build_keilan_cloud_card_textures.py` | per-variant manifest and review sheet |
| Build pairwise seam-safe horizon set | `scripts/build_seam_safe_horizon_cloud_card_set.py` | schema-8 A/B manifests, pair manifest, direct-R6 interior and transparent-neutral audits |
| Verify packed alpha/density/mips | `scripts/qa_cloud_card_alpha_mips.py` | per-variant QA and combined pass summary |
| Review the A/B cycle | `scripts/review_keilan_horizon_cloud_set.py` | shared QA JSON and `A-B-A-B` review |
| Review live gameplay-height response | `scripts/review_cloud_bake_showcase_play_ue.py` | eight captures, projected-card ROI response gates, contact sheet, and JSON manifest |

The workflow contract, not a script's generic default, is authoritative. Until
the tools consume one shared versioned profile, a distant-horizon pack must
explicitly use `--size 4096x1024 --max-background-median-srgb 0.16`. Feed only
the exact preprojected basis sources and verify in the manifest that every
alignment scale is `[1,1]`, every offset is `[0,0]`, and every post-alignment
IoU is `1.0`.

The accepted
`SourceArt/Clouds/Cumulus_01/KeilanCardBake/TiledHorizonCumulus_Bright_Keilan_v02`
set is the first distant-horizon regression fixture. Future tool changes must
compare against it without replacing its accepted source history.

## Open incubation backlog

The following items block formal-skill promotion. Keep them visible until
implemented and proven:

- Replace conflicting generic defaults with versioned Single Cloud and Distant
  Horizon profiles. The distant profile must own its 4096x1024 size,
  `RGB(0,17,38)` background, thresholds, and exact-basis policy.
- Move background estimation, signal-mask extraction, thresholds, and channel
  semantics into one shared contract module used by every stage.
- Add default no-clobber behavior, revision directories, temporary staging,
  and atomic publication so a failed run cannot damage an accepted set or
  leave partial production output.
- Chain stages through schema-validated run manifests. Each stage must verify
  the previous stage's report and hashes rather than trusting paths alone.
- Add a strict preprojected-basis pack mode that forbids geometry resampling
  and requires exact Beauty support instead of merely accepting a loose IoU.
- Add harmonization approval gates for actual exposure/chroma improvement,
  gamut-limited pixels, and threshold-recovery pixels. A no-op correction must
  not pass merely because it preserved geometry.
- Add basis approval gates for overlap, alignment confidence, meaningful
  directional diversity, gain limits, and centered mean energy. Three
  identical or ineffective basis images must fail.
- Extend final QA to inspect `StaticBasisRGBA` and `LightDataRGBA`, cross-family
  alpha equality, fixed background, A/B exposure and chroma, and far-layer
  hierarchy—not only source and packed Beauty.
- Produce explicit 100%, 50%, 25%, and 12.5% reviews over dark matte and the
  actual target sky. Preserve the human visual verdict beside machine gates.
- Add representative self-tests for every stage and end-to-end regression
  tests for both pipeline routes.
- Bring Single Cloud automation to the same deterministic level as Distant
  Horizon. If that is not achieved, promote a narrower distant-horizon skill
  first instead of claiming that one skill fully supports both routes.

## Formal-skill promotion gates

Do not create or install the formal skill merely because one asset passed.
Promote only when all of the following are true:

- At least two visually distinct, accepted production examples exist for each
  pipeline route.
- The complete route can be repeated without an undocumented manual image,
  path, or editor step.
- Every deterministic script has tested CLI behavior, actionable failures, and
  machine-readable reports.
- Raw ImageGen calls, normalized sources, corrections, packed outputs, and
  Unreal assets can be traced by path and hash.
- Coordinate conversion, SDF settings, image color space, channel contracts,
  texture settings, and Unreal placement rules are verified end to end.
- Unreal import and runtime/cook behavior pass without a persisted UnrealMCP
  dependency.
- Common failure modes and recovery choices have been observed and documented
  from real work.
- A fresh agent can select the correct route, produce the expected
  deliverables, and interpret failures using only the proposed skill.
- A machine-QA-passing candidate has been visually reviewed in the target sky,
  and the user has explicitly accepted its appearance and default parameters.
- The user explicitly declares the workflow complete and approves skill
  promotion.

At promotion time, initialize a concise skill rather than copying this entire
development document into `SKILL.md`. Use this intended resource shape:

```text
cubeless-cloud-card-baking/
├── SKILL.md
├── agents/openai.yaml
├── scripts/
│   ├── run_pipeline.py
│   ├── normalize_horizon_set.py
│   ├── harmonize_horizon_set.py
│   ├── project_basis_lighting.py
│   ├── pack_cloud_card.py
│   ├── review_horizon_set.py
│   ├── validate_run.py
│   ├── lib/
│   │   └── cloud_card_contract.py
│   └── tests/
├── assets/
│   └── profiles/
│       ├── distant-horizon-v1.json
│       └── single-cloud-v1.json
└── references/
    ├── single-cloud.md
    ├── distant-horizon.md
    ├── channel-and-unreal-contracts.md
    ├── qa-and-promotion.md
    └── failure-modes.md
```

Keep `SKILL.md` focused on route selection, execution order, and mandatory
gates. Keep detailed contracts and failure evidence in the one-level
`references/` files. Keep numeric tuning in versioned profiles rather than
hard-coding it in `SKILL.md`. Do not place this incubation history, a README,
or a separate changelog inside the final skill.

## Routing checklist

Choose Single Cloud when any answer is yes:

- Is one recognizable silhouette the subject?
- Must the cloud be viewed or rotated as an individual asset?
- Does the source require Hunyuan geometry or SDF volume authoring?

Choose Distant Horizon when all answers are yes:

- Is the asset viewed primarily as a long horizontal skyline band?
- Is hiding horizontal repetition more important than preserving one cloud?
- Can placement obey the fixed A/B cycle?
- Can the final result remain a camera-facing distant card?

Do not convert a single-cloud asset into a distant tile by merely copying or
shrinking it. Do not convert a distant A/B set into a hero cloud by cropping
one landmark from it.

### R19 dense-body slope-relaxation candidate (`incubation-r16`, 2026-08-02)

The Leaning Trail R19 candidate entered the pipeline as a create-only bake
experiment. It always
reconstructs from accepted R6 plus its clean aligned reference; it never edits
R18 cumulatively. The selected `Recommended` variant combines the bounded R18
highlight pull with a small low-frequency slope relaxation and achieved an
11.77 percent macro-gradient reduction while retaining 0.998587 microdetail
correlation and 1.94 percent p99 peak loss.

The protection contract is stricter than the visual objective: Beauty alpha,
StaticBasis, and LightData are byte exact; alpha below 64, the first six
silhouette pixels, and the reviewed lower-underside mask have zero changed
pixels. The Unreal candidate uses the R17 soft-rim master and both R16/R17
structure masks at the unchanged 349 VS / 839 PS / 4 sample / 6 sampler cost.
It remained review-only through `incubation-r16`; the user-approved production
promotion is recorded in `incubation-r18` below.

### Wide Cumulus R19 plus R17 extension (`incubation-r17`, 2026-08-02)

The Wide Cumulus card used by
`BP_WideCumulusBank_Bright_R6_DirectionalRim_R15Candidate` now has the same
create-only R19 Beauty and R17 soft-rim treatment as the Leaning Trail. The
reviewed R15 BP, MI, level actor, accepted R6 pack, and shared R17 master were
immutable review inputs; the later user-approved replacement is recorded in
`incubation-r18` below.

- The authoritative offline Beauty is the `R19SlopeRelaxR2Candidate`
  Recommended variant. It reduces the dense-body macro gradient by 12.339
  percent with 0.997689 microdetail correlation, 0.005105 mean absolute
  opaque Y change, 0.055 p99 absolute change, and 2.152 percent p99 peak loss.
  Beauty alpha, StaticBasis, and LightData remain byte exact. Alpha below 64,
  the first six silhouette pixels, the reviewed underside, and every protected
  pixel have zero edits.
- The Wide-specific R16/R17 V3 masks use the clean aligned source only as
  contour authority, then clip both final masks by accepted R6 alpha. This
  avoids treating the source's rectangular transparent padding and right-hand
  shelf artifact as rim structure without changing opacity or creating energy
  outside the accepted card. The hard mask covers 210,270 texels; the soft
  pointwise-bounded subset covers 126,098 texels, has no full-white texels, and
  has zero support expansion, hard/soft low-alpha leakage, brighter-than-hard
  texels, or non-black 24-pixel border texels. Earlier V1/V2 masks remain only
  as rejected evidence because their contours followed the padded alpha
  topology too literally.
- The UE candidate lives under
  `/Game/Study/SKY_Cloud/StaticCloudCard/BeautyBakeR19WideSoftRimCandidate`.
  Its MI preserves 59 effective R15 parameters except the intentional Beauty
  replacement, its BP preserves 27 actor defaults except Beauty and
  MaterialTemplate, and both R16/R17 static switches are enabled. The compiled
  cost is 349 VS / 839 PS / 4 texture samples / 6 samplers versus the R15
  source's 349 / 816 / 3 / 5. BP compilation has zero errors and warnings, and
  dependency audit finds no UnrealMCP runtime reference.
- The fixed Wide-card review uses one existing R15 actor and a transient
  candidate MID at 841x572 under front, back, back-left, and back-right light.
  Every row is captured as baseline A1, candidate B, restored baseline A2.
  Candidate changed-fraction above 2 u8 is 0.0894, 3.3208, 1.1119, and 1.5520
  percent respectively, concentrating the useful change in reverse-light
  conditions. A1/A2 restoration stays at p95 1 u8, mean absolute 0.1177-0.1196
  u8, and at most 0.0048 percent above 2 u8, matching the measured active
  viewport/TAA floor rather than indicating a material restore failure.
- Capture restores the exact R15 MID, light rotation, actor transform,
  temporary visibility, -0.5 EV manual exposure, CloudBakeSky MPC values, and
  dirty map/content package sets. It does not save the map or replace the R15
  actor. A stale starting MPC sun-direction cache must be restored explicitly
  after `RefreshFromSceneLights`; merely restoring the light is not a complete
  state-neutral review contract.

Deterministic scripts and evidence:

- `scripts/build_widecumulusbank_bright_slope_relaxed_beauty_r19.py`
- `scripts/build_widecumulus_r17_rim_masks.py`
- `scripts/stage_widecumulus_r19_r17_soft_rim_candidate_ue.py`
- `scripts/capture_widecumulus_r15_r19_r17_review_ue.py`
- `output/widecumulus_r15_r19_r17_live_review_20260802/`

### Two-card production library (`incubation-r18`, 2026-08-02)

After user acceptance, the Static Cloud Card production library was reduced to
two concrete cloud children:

- `BeautyBakeR19SlopeRelaxSoftRimCandidate/BP_LeaningCumulusTrail_Bright_R6UnderFeatherB60_ID112_4K_R19SlopeRelaxCandidate_R17SoftRim`
- `BeautyBakeR19WideSoftRimCandidate/BP_WideCumulusBank_Bright_R6_R19SlopeRelaxR2_R17SoftRimCandidate`

`Sky_Cloud_Map` contains exactly these two card actors under
`SkyBake/ApprovedCards`; all 19 legacy/review card placements were replaced.
The asset-root audit went from 88 assets to a 32-asset protected dependency
closure, retiring 56 obsolete BP/MI/material/texture assets. The closure keeps
the shared base/dome infrastructure, SkyBake/Wisp assets, R17 material and
masks, and the exact packed inputs required by the two cards. Offline source
art and review evidence remain outside the Unreal asset library.

`BP_StaticCloudCard` has 29 declared artist parameters. Graph and child-default
audits proved that all 29 are consumed and already instance-editable, so none
were removed or newly exposed. The two approved children declare no additional
local parameters. This 29-parameter parent contract is now the cleanup guard:
do not infer that a parameter is unused merely because one of the two child
CDOs leaves it at the parent default.

Deterministic cleanup and proof are stored in:

- `scripts/cleanup_static_cloud_card_library_ue.py`
- `output/cloud_card_cleanup_20260802/cleanup_manifest.json`

